From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Newport <kethinov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 20:15:00 -0400
Subject: fix: do not skip still-launching renderers when initializing
 spellcheck

SpellcheckService::InitForAllRenderers() gates on
RenderProcessHost::GetProcess().Handle(), which is null for a renderer
that has been initialized but whose process is still launching. Such a
renderer is silently skipped and never receives the notification again.

That matters because InitForAllRenderers() is the sole repair path for a
renderer that was initialized before its dictionaries were ready. Since
Chromium 143 (crbug.com/448511116) OnRenderProcessHostCreated() is
dispatched from RenderProcessHostImpl::Init() rather than from
OnProcessLaunched(), so InitForRenderer() now runs before the renderer
process exists. If the Hunspell dictionaries are still loading off disk at
that point the renderer is handed a dictionary entry holding an invalid
base::File; HunspellEngine::Init() latches initialized_ = true with
hunspell_enabled_ = false, and because dictionary_requested_ is already
set it never asks for the dictionary again. The subsequent
OnHunspellDictionaryInitialized() -> InitForAllRenderers() is supposed to
hand it the real file, but that is exactly the call the handle check
throws away.

Whether the dictionary load wins the race against the renderer launch
depends on how long the .bdic takes to become available: a download takes
long enough that the renderer is up by the time it lands, while a
dictionary already cached on disk from a previous run loads in a few
milliseconds and reliably lands inside the launch window. So spellcheck
works on an app's first run and is dead on every run after, until
something else happens to call InitForAllRenderers() -- which is why
toggling the spellcheck.enable pref off and on is a workaround.

Test IsInitializedAndNotDead() instead, which is what
OnCustomDictionaryChanged() already uses to iterate the same hosts for the
same purpose.

Upstreamed at https://crrev.com/f7aaf9a09a06e77292ea077bcd1527034d02f449
so this patch can be removed once Chromium rolls past that revision.

Refs https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/50327

diff --git a/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_service.cc b/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_service.cc
index d47c9adff7b4c7cbeacb050119eb7c5d1acf34c2..c739fa151c8e79ed725e4e4755449808b1f35953 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_service.cc
@@ -965,8 +965,14 @@ void SpellcheckService::InitForAllRenderers() {
   for (auto it = content::RenderProcessHost::AllHostsIterator(); !it.IsAtEnd();
        it.Advance()) {
     content::RenderProcessHost* process = it.GetCurrentValue();
-    if (process && process->GetProcess().Handle())
+    // Do not test GetProcess().Handle() here: a renderer that has been
+    // initialized but whose process is still launching has no handle yet, and
+    // skipping it drops the notification for good. Its mojo channel already
+    // exists, so messages queue up and are delivered once the process is up.
+    // This matches OnCustomDictionaryChanged() below.
+    if (process && process->IsInitializedAndNotDead()) {
       InitForRenderer(process);
+    }
   }
 }
 
